# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What does NOT belong in this repository.
#
# The site itself has no build step and no dependencies, so this list is short
# by design: everything here is either a machine artefact, a local log, or an
# archive of the folder that lives beside it. Nothing the site serves is
# ignored — if a browser asks for it, it is committed.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python bytecode, written whenever tools/trace-bismillah.py or
# tools/build-fonts.py is run.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Written by tools/refresh-scholar.ps1, one line per run. It is a record of
# what this machine did, not of what the site is — and two machines refreshing
# the snapshot would conflict on it for no reason. README §11.4C.
tools/scholar-refresh.log

# Playwright, if you install it to run the browser-driven guards
# (check-ui, check-canary, check-farsi, check-contrast, check-dropcap).
# README §11.4D has the one-line install.
#
# package.json is ignored too, deliberately. `npm i -D playwright` writes a
# three-line manifest whose only content is that optional dev dependency, and
# committing it would turn a folder you can upload to any static host into an
# npm project — including on the university server, where it means nothing.
# The site itself still has no build step and no dependencies, which is the
# claim §1 and §11 make and the one worth keeping true. Install Playwright
# when you want to run the guards; nothing about the site needs it.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# The dated .rar snapshots of this folder, and any editor or OS leavings.
*.rar
*.zip
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# Local preview configuration for the editor's dev-server launcher.
.claude/
